# Entrega (fonte oficial)

This is the official delivery architecture. Seeds, migrations, refactors, deploys, and new features must not replace it. If a new feature conflicts, the feature adapts to this rule.

1. Coverage = point inside the green polygon. Outside = "Não entregamos nesta região."
2. Fee = KM tier table from store to that point. Never area `minFee`/`feePerKm` when tiers exist. Never neighborhood zone fees while áreas or KM are on.
3. Typed address, GPS, and map pin all call `applyCoordinates` → `validateDeliveryCoverage(lat, lng)`. Same point, same result.
4. `seed.ts` must never insert `DEFAULT_DELIVERY_ZONES` or any bairro list. If `areasEnabled`, leftover `delivery_zones` are deleted on boot so they cannot return after deploy.
5. Do not geocode to a namesake in another neighborhood (Portão vs Itinga) or to Lauro city centroid. Unmapped real streets: GPS or map pin, never invented coordinates.
6. Street registry and old bairro fees cannot overwrite an allowed polygon/KM result.

Keep `scripts/gps-delivery-coverage-selftest.mjs` and `scripts/delivery-areas-resolve-selftest.mjs` passing.
